# Colophon

## Backend

This website is a collection of static HTML pages generated by a custom
[site generator][ssg]. It is a VM on "someone else's computer" running
[OpenBSD][]. The pages are served by [relayd][], and [httpd][]. 
The entire content of the site can be found in a [git repository](https://gith
ub.com/e-zk/site).

A [hidden service][hiddenservices] mirror of this site is available and can be
accessed at the following onion address: 
[64wv2uqwjacqer7z5d6ooqgrvjwlioizmo7hgmxm7zxerbvgnoqhafid.onion](http://64wv2u
qwjacqer7z5d6ooqgrvjwlioizmo7hgmxm7zxerbvgnoqhafid.onion).

[ssg]: https://github.com/e-zk/site-gen/
[OpenBSD]: https://openbsd.org/
[relayd]: https://man.openbsd.org/relayd
[httpd]: https://man.openbsd.org/httpd
[vis]: https://github.com/martanne/vis
[hiddenservices]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tor_(network)#Onion_services
[djot]: https://djot.net/

## Writing

Posts are edited in the [vis editor][vis] as Markdown, or more recently,
[djot][] files.  
In the footer of most pages, you can open the plaintext representation. I try
to keep the text width under 80 characters for readability. \
I sometimes run longer posts through `aspell` to check spelling,
but not always.

## Design

I handwrite the [CSS](/style.css) here. I do enjoy playing with CSS so you'll
find the layout, style, fonts, colours for this site will change pretty often.
I muck about with CSS more than I actually write content for the site.

## Typography

As of writing, this site is using your defaults for 'serif', and 'monospace'
fonts. I think this is sufficient for readability; seems to look okay-ish
on most system's defaults. I'm often torn between importing nicer looking
fonts and also maintaining the simplicity and "lightweight"-ness of the site.

## JavaScript

I don't use any JavaScript on the site.

## Tracking

I don't do any analytics or tracking for your visits, but I do have access
logs for the site somewhere around here. I've never had to dig into them.
Now I'm curious what they look like...

## AI

I don't use any AI/LLMs to generate the code, or content on this site.
